# Phase 15 – Server Migration & Dynamic Configuration

This phase implements a robust Remote Configuration Service and dynamic configuration endpoints to allow updating server URLs, feature flags, carousel configurations, and maintenance mode status without releasing a new mobile application build. Additionally, it implements a failover server switching strategy on the mobile client.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Anonymous Remote Config Access:** The Remote Config endpoint `/api/v1/config/features` will be accessible anonymously (unauthenticated) to allow the app to fetch server endpoints and check maintenance mode before logging in or on first launch.

> [!NOTE]
> **Transparent Failover Interceptor:** The failover server switching logic is implemented directly as a Dio interceptor. If any API request fails due to connection loss/timeout, the interceptor will automatically ping alternative server endpoints, switch to a working host, update the cached endpoint, and retry the request transparently.

## Open Questions
There are no open questions; the architecture aligns cleanly with client expectations.

